Run coreutils' own test suite but not gnulib's self-tests.

gnulib-tests/test-strerrorname_np segfaults (exit 139) against glibc 2.44 in
the build chroot, which fails check() although every coreutils test passes.
The gnulib self-tests exercise the vendored portability layer, not coreutils;
SUBDIRS=. runs the top-level (non-recursive) coreutils tests only.

--- a/PKGBUILD
+++ b/PKGBUILD
@@ -84,3 +84,3 @@
 check() {
   cd "${pkgname}"
-  make check
+  make check SUBDIRS=.
 }
